{"step_index":1336,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:45:09Z","thinking":"**Examining Candidate Proof Feasibility**\n\nAssess whether `Candidate` can be proven within Lean 4. Specifically, investigate the definition of `Candidate`. It's defined as a proposition involving graphs, their properties, and associated mathematical concepts. The core of this involves checking if the given condition is provable.\n\n\n**Analyzing Proof Structure**\n\nThe proof strategy seems to involve casework on the cardinality of the vertex set and the graph's radius, along with the roman weight of a function. Several lemmas appear to be invoked depending on these conditions. Initial hypothesis is that the cardinality of the vertex set is less than or equal to the roman weight, thus invoking `radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_card_le`.\n\n\n**Investigating Proof Strategy Refinement**\n\nFocusing on the goal `radius G + 1 ≤ romanWeight f`, explore available lemmas. Recalling `radius_add_one_le_card` provides a potential upper bound. Further consideration needed on whether a connection can be established between romanWeight and radius, particularly given the condition `radius G ≥ 4`. The prior work in `test_full.lean` and `Challenge_e20263a9.lean` appears incomplete.\n\n\n**Refining Proof Strategy**\n\nThe definitions of `romanDominationNumber` and `radius` are in a custom project; Mathlib doesn't offer direct theorems linking them. The goal is to prove `radius G + 1 ≤ romanWeight f`, exploring the lemma `radius_add_one_le_of_card_compl`. This lemma provides a condition: if there exist $v, k$ such that $k + (V \\setminus B_k(v)).card + 1 ≤ W$, then radius G + 1 ≤ W.\n\nSetting `v` as a center of the graph, and k equal to the radius gives $V \\setminus B_k(v) = \\emptyset$, so $(V \\setminus B_k(v)).card = 0$. This simplifies the condition in the `radius_add_one_le_of_card_compl` lemma to `radius(G) + 1 ≤ W`, which aligns directly with the original proof objective. The condition trivially holds by choosing W = romanWeight f.\n\n\n**Analyzing Roman Domination Relationships**\n\nExamined the relationship between graph radius and R\n<truncated 23569 bytes>\n converted to Lean 4, then the `sorry` block will be removed.\n\n**Exploring Formalization of Logic**\n\nConsidered how to formulate the statement \"For every connected graph G and every Roman dominating function f\" within the Lean 4 environment. Identified that such formalization relies on the appropriate type classes or structures for connected graphs and Roman dominating functions.\n\n**Implementing Proof Strategy**\n\nFocused on formalizing the proof strategy. If `radius(G) <= romanWeight(f) - 1`, this implies `radius G + 1 <= romanWeight f`.  This inequality will be the core of the proof.\n\n**Preparing Proof Construction**\n\nPreparing a Lean 4 Lemma that will capture `radius G + 1 <= romanWeight f`, for all graphs and roman dominating functions. The Lemma will define all variables, and then the logic can be applied to replace the `sorry` statement.\n\n\n**Analyzing Ball Properties for Proof**\n\nConsidered using the lemma `ballWithin_univ_or_card_ge`. Determined that either `B_{romanWeight(f) - 1}(v) = univ` or `|B_{romanWeight(f) - 1}(v)| ≥ romanWeight(f)`. If at least one vertex's ball equals the universe, the proof is immediate. Explored the case where all balls are not the universe, leading to `radius(G) + 1 > romanWeight(f)` which would create a contradiction.\n\n**Connecting Ball Cardinality and Proof Goal**\n\nInvestigated under what conditions `B_m(v) = univ`. Recognized `B_{k + m}(v) = univ` if `|V| ≤ |B_k(v)| + m` using `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_card_add`. Chose `m = |V| - |B_k(v)|` leading to `eccentricity(v) ≤ k + |V| - |B_k(v)|`.\n\n**Establishing Ball Cardinality Condition**\n\nTo achieve the goal, focused on finding a `v` and `k` with `k + |V| - |B_k(v)| ≤ romanWeight(f) - 1`. This leads to `|B_k(v)| ≥ |V| - romanWeight(f) + k + 1`.\n\n**Examining Neighborhood Relationships**\n\nConsidered the neighborhood of two vertices u1 and u2 labeled 2, observing every vertex with label 0 is in the neighborhood of $u_1$ or $u_2$. Explored relationships between the neighborhoods of these vertices to achieve the proof goal.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh\"","ContentOffset":"0","EndLine":"100","StartLine":"1","toolAction":"\"Viewing check.sh\"","toolSummary":"\"View check.sh script\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking"]}
{"step_index":1337,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:46:06Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:46:06+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:46:06+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh`\nTotal Lines: 51\nTotal Bytes: 2182\nShowing lines 1 to 51\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: #!/bin/bash\n2: # check.sh — the ONLY command an agent may run.\n3: #\n4: #   /abs/path/tools/antigravity/check.sh FILE.lean\n5: #\n6: # Lives outside every agent workspace and is hashed by guard.sh: agents can\n7: # write inside their workspace, so a checker kept there could be rewritten into\n8: # anything. It screens the file first (tools/antigravity_handoff.py lint), because\n9: # Lean elaboration can itself run shell commands; then elaborates it with bare\n10: # `lean` and an explicit LEAN_PATH, and prints every theorem's axioms. Nothing\n11: # here depends on $HOME — agents run under a private one — and `lake` is never\n12: # involved (in this project lake deletes Mathlib when it cannot re-clone).\n13: set -uo pipefail\n14: f=\"${1:?usage: check.sh FILE.lean}\"\n15: [ -f \"$f\" ] || { echo \"CHECK: no such file: $f\"; exit 2; }\n16: \n17: ROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$(readlink -f \"$0\")\")/../..\" && pwd)\"\n18: # Tool paths come from a protected file, not from the home directory: agents run\n19: # under a private HOME, and on compute nodes `getent passwd` reports a different\n20: # home (/home/<user>@ad…) than the one the tools live in.\n21: ENVF=\"$ROOT/handoff/.agf_env\"\n22: export ELAN_HOME=\"$(grep -m1 '^AGF_ELAN_HOME=' \"$ENVF\" 2>/dev/null | cut -d= -f2-)\"\n23: LEAN=\"$ELAN_HOME/bin/lean\"\n24: [ -x \"$LEAN\" ] || { echo \"CHECK: lean not found (ELAN_HOME='$ELAN_HOME' from $ENVF)\"; exit 2; }\n25: PY=\"$ROOT/.venv/bin/python\"\n26: LP_FILE=\"$ROOT/handoff/.agf_lean_path\"\n27: [ -s \"$LP_FILE\" ] || { echo \"CHECK: missing $LP_FILE\"; exit 2; }\n28: export LEAN_PATH=\"$(cat \"$LP_FILE\")\"\n29: \n30: orig=\"$(ls \"$ROOT\"/benchmark/challenges_*/\"$(basename \"$f\")\" 2>/dev/null | head -1)\"\n31: if ! \"$PY\" \"$ROOT/tools/antigravity_handoff.py\" lint ${orig:+--original \"$orig\"} \"$f\"; then\n32:   echo \"CHECK: refused to elaborate — remove the construct named above.\"\n33:   exit 3\n34: fi\n35: \n36: tmp=\"$(mktemp --suffix=.lean)\"\n37: cp \"$f\" \"$tmp\"\n38: for t in $(grep -oE '^theorem +[A-Za-z0-9_]+' \"$f\" | awk '{print $2}'); do\n39:   echo \"#print axioms $t\" >> \"$tmp\"\n40: done\n41: timeout 1800 \"$LEAN\" \"$tmp\"\n42: rc=$?\n43: rm -f \"$tmp\"\n44: if [ $rc -eq 0 ]; then\n45:   echo \"CHECK: elaborated. Allowed axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound.\"\n46:   echo \"       'sorryAx' in a list above means that theorem is unfinished.\"\n47: else\n48:   echo \"CHECK: FAILED (exit $rc)\"\n49: fi\n50: exit $rc\n51: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
