{"step_index":1343,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:46:14Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:46:14+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:46:14+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity_handoff.py`\nTotal Lines: 348\nTotal Bytes: 15551\nShowing lines 100 to 200\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n100: \n101: \n102: # ── admissibility ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n103: #\n104: # An answer is compiled as the *returned file*, helper lemmas included — pasting\n105: # only the proof body back into the original, as the model campaign did, drops\n106: # every lemma a real proof needs and turns a correct proof into \"unresolved\".\n107: #\n108: # Compiling the returned file is only sound if nothing in it can change what is\n109: # being proved. The checks below close the routes that exist in Lean for that:\n110: # editing `Candidate` or anything it elaborates against; extending its term past\n111: # where it ended (a term does not stop at a newline); re-declaring `Candidate` or\n112: # the target inside a namespace; adding `variable` hypotheses the target silently\n113: # absorbs; redefining the tokens `Candidate` parses as; and bypassing the kernel.\n114: # The target's type is then re-checked by Lean itself, and the axiom audit rejects\n115: # `sorryAx` and anything non-standard.\n116: \n117: _CMD_START = (\"theorem\", \"lemma\", \"def\", \"abbrev\", \"example\", \"instance\", \"open\",\n118:               \"set_option\", \"attribute\", \"noncomputable\", \"private\", \"protected\",\n119:               \"@[\", \"#check\", \"#print\", \"structure\", \"inductive\", \"class\")\n120: \n121: _FORBIDDEN_CMD = re.compile(\n122:     r\"(?m)^\\s*(?:(?:p