uded that |V2| must be greater or equal to 2. Checked the case radius(G) ≤ 3, leading to a contradiction. Deducted that radius(G) ≥ 4, and therefore W ≥ 5. Also, observed that W < radius(G) + 1.\n\n**Developing a proof strategy**\n\nConsidering if it is possible to demonstrate that, for any Roman dominating function and any graph: radius(G) + 1 ≤ romanWeight(f). Attempting to formulate a lemma for connected graphs to prove this inequality. Exploring tactics like `omega` and `linarith` to establish the inequalities.\n\n**Identifying potential lemmas**\n\nExploring the potential lemma from `radius_add_one_le` and where this could lead in Lean4. The key is in combining inequalities to prove the overall target inequality.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/Challenge_e20263a9.lean\"","ContentOffset":"0","EndLine":"70","StartLine":"15","toolAction":"\"Viewing Challenge_e20263a9.lean lines 15-70\"","toolSummary":"\"View Challenge_e20263a9.lean lines 15-70\""}}]}
